{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "enpe7n1le02ob09re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "The History of Minicomputers ", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 12, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n1le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "100", "text": "<strong>Sophia</strong>: Were you able to read about microcomputers yesterday?<br>\n<strong>Jeffery</strong>:  Yes. Let's review what we read in the article. Why were microcomputers a good idea? <br>\n<strong>Sophia</strong>: Computers were first designed for governments and large corporations. However, some people in the industry thought that computers didn't need to be so exclusive. Computers were very expensive and big, so developers had to find a way to reduce the price and size. So, they had to face the big question: How can we make computers more affordable? Their solution was to replace the vacuum tubes with transistorized models for making smaller and cheaper computers. <br>", "image": "enpe7n1le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "47000", "text": "<strong>Jeffery</strong>: Can a solution like this make a real difference? <br>\n<strong>Sophia</strong>: Certainly. The innovative microcomputers brought a new class of users. After that, scientists and engineers were able to afford computers. <br>\n<strong>Jeffery</strong>: How were these new computers innovative? <br>\n<strong>Sophia</strong>: Thanks to the new technology and the economies of scale, the prices of microcomputers decreased and by 1970 there were around 50 companies making microcomputers. These technology advances are still very important today. <br>\n<strong>Jeffery</strong>: Were these minicomputers used only by scientists and engineers? <br>", "image": "enpe7n1le02ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "87800", "text": "<strong>Sophia</strong>: At the beginning, they were. However, during the 1980s, computers were small and cheap enough for making them affordable for individuals. <br>\n<strong>Jeffery</strong>: How were they able to create more affordable computers? <br>\n<strong>Sophia</strong>: It was thanks to the invention of the integrated circuit. Many transistors were included in a single chip of silicon, making computers smaller and affordable for individuals. <br>\n<strong>Jeffery</strong>: How can integrated circuits make computers smaller? <br>\n<strong>Sophia</strong>: It's simple. As more transistors fit in a smaller space, computer memory, logic circuits, and other components take less room, and computers become smaller.", "image": "enpe7n1le02ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n1le02ob09re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "id": 1, "type": "audio"}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}